DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program re-runs a typescript, using stdin typescript and timing
       information to ensure that input happens in the same rhythm as it
       originally appeared when the script was recorded.

       The sseessssiioonn iiss eexxeeccuutteedd in a newly created pseudoterminal with the
       user’s $SHELL (or defaults to _/_b_i_n_/_b_a_s_h).

       BBee ccaarreeffuull!! Do not forget that the typescript may contains arbitrary
       commands. It is recommended to use ""ssccrriippttrreeppllaayy ----ssttrreeaamm iinn ----lloogg--iinn
       ttyyppeessccrriipptt"" (or with ----lloogg--iioo instead of ----lloogg--iinn) to verify the
       typescript before it is executed by ssccrriippttlliivvee.

       The timing information is what ssccrriipptt(1) outputs to file specified by
       ----lloogg--ttiimmiinngg. The typescript has to contain stdin information and it is
       what script1 outputs to file specified by ----lloogg--iinn or ----lloogg--iioo.

